(1918724, 259117, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Great idea for the cheater challenge. It was such a great idea a thousand people did it. Not that I think thats bad for you, but it does seem to bore the voters as they look through 200 images to see the same idea over and over. For starters, there is nothing in focus. Your contrast looks good, but I think that the photo would have been better in color. I don''t say that very often because I love bw. BW is great when there is alot of texture present and since this really doesn''t have any, I would have chosen color. Poker chips are so colorful as well as cards, it would have been more appealing that way. As for you set-up of the shot, I think that you did well. You have the Ace hidden nicely in the cuff of the shirt, and I like the placement of the chips and deck of cards. You have a great camera and if I knew anything about it I would give you suggestions on how to get a better focused shot. With my camera, I would have had to use the macro setting to get a focused shot of your image. Hope this was helpful and I am glad you are entering challenges again. Welcome back to the insanity!!<br/> <br/>Mandy</td>', '*Critique Club* Great idea for the cheater challenge. It was such a great idea a thousand people did it. Not that I think thats bad for you, but it does seem to bore the voters as they look through 200 images to see the same idea over and over. For starters, there is nothing in focus. Your contrast looks good, but I think that the photo would have been better in color. I don''t say that very often because I love bw. BW is great when there is alot of texture present and since this really doesn''t have any, I would have chosen color. Poker chips are so colorful as well as cards, it would have been more appealing that way. As for you set-up of the shot, I think that you did well. You have the Ace hidden nicely in the cuff of the shirt, and I like the placement of the chips and deck of cards. You have a great camera and if I knew anything about it I would give you suggestions on how to get a better focused shot. With my camera, I would have had to use the macro setting to get a focused shot of your image. Hope this was helpful and I am glad you are entering challenges again. Welcome back to the insanity!! Mandy', '2005-12-03 10:08:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1918747, 259858, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>I love this. I feel that it fits the challenge so well. Very refreshing to see a different idea other than playing cards. The fog is just right. You can see the photographer well enough to see that he is kind of bumbed out because he is not going to get the shot he wanted. Man, we have all been there a time or two. I love this picture. Perfect for a DPC challenge. Even though I see the relation to the theme, others did not. I think that sometimes people have a certain idea of what the theme is and see nothing beyond that. Everyone thinks differently ya know? Great picture. Great picture. Keep thinking out of the box. <br/> <br/>Mandy</td>', '*Critique Club* I love this. I feel that it fits the challenge so well. Very refreshing to see a different idea other than playing cards. The fog is just right. You can see the photographer well enough to see that he is kind of bumbed out because he is not going to get the shot he wanted. Man, we have all been there a time or two. I love this picture. Perfect for a DPC challenge. Even though I see the relation to the theme, others did not. I think that sometimes people have a certain idea of what the theme is and see nothing beyond that. Everyone thinks differently ya know? Great picture. Great picture. Keep thinking out of the box.  Mandy', '2005-12-03 10:23:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1918771, 259513, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Great idea for the challenge. The lighting is very harsh. Would have been more believable as a cheater if the man was wearing a wedding ring. Would have liked to see the faces more. You look very romatically dressed, but he does not. That is just something I noticed. Would have fit the title better if one of you was trying to hurry up and leave (standing up) but grabbed each other for one more kiss. The sitting down position doesn''t look very romantic. Would have been better if you were barefooted also. Of course these are all just my opinions and everyone has a different point of view. I hope this wasn''t too harsh, just trying to give my honest opinion of your entry. Good luck in future challenges.<br/> <br/>Mandy</td>', '*Critique Club* Great idea for the challenge. The lighting is very harsh. Would have been more believable as a cheater if the man was wearing a wedding ring. Would have liked to see the faces more. You look very romatically dressed, but he does not. That is just something I noticed. Would have fit the title better if one of you was trying to hurry up and leave (standing up) but grabbed each other for one more kiss. The sitting down position doesn''t look very romantic. Would have been better if you were barefooted also. Of course these are all just my opinions and everyone has a different point of view. I hope this wasn''t too harsh, just trying to give my honest opinion of your entry. Good luck in future challenges. Mandy', '2005-12-03 10:35:23.000000', NULL, 0),
